# Keep host build artifacts out of the Docker build context.
#
# Without this, `COPY apps/frontend/ ./` drags in the developer's compiled
# `vite.config.js` — a gitignored artifact of `tsc -b` — which Vite loads in
# preference to `vite.config.ts`, so the image built from a stale config (or
# failed outright). It also copied host `node_modules`, built for the
# developer's platform, over the Linux install from `npm ci`.
#
# Note: `src/api/generated.ts` is gitignored but *is* required by the build,
# so it is deliberately not excluded here.

# Dependencies and virtualenvs — reinstalled inside the image
**/node_modules
**/.venv

# Build output — produced inside the image
**/dist
apps/frontend/vite.config.js
apps/frontend/vite.config.d.ts
apps/frontend/*.tsbuildinfo

# Python caches and local state
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
apps/backend/.dev-data
apps/backend/.dev-config

# Repo tooling and local scratch, none of which the image needs
.git
.github
.worktrees
.superpowers
.playwright-mcp
docs
.env
